<BaseLayout title="Job Opportunity Engine — Governed career operations" description="A private, local-first governed career-operations system for deterministic evaluation, evidence-bound preparation, and human review.">
  <article class="joe-case-study">
    <header class="joe-hero shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Case study · private system</p>
      <h1>Job Opportunity<br />Engine</h1>
      <p class="joe-subtitle">Governed career operations for collection, deterministic evaluation, evidence-bound preparation, and human review.</p>
      <div class="joe-hero-grid">
        <p class="joe-summary">A career workflow should not treat a persuasive sentence as candidate truth. Job Opportunity Engine is a private, local-first governed career-operations system spanning job collection, deterministic evaluation, evidence-bound preparation, private artifact custody, and human review.</p>
        <dl class="joe-facts"><div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Product architecture, governance, requirements, and technical-program direction</dd></div><div><dt>Current state</dt><dd>Private Python + SQLite implementation with preparation and review controls</dd></div></dl>
      </div>
      <aside class="authority-ledger authority-ledger-joe" aria-label="Job Opportunity Engine authority ledger"><p class="eyebrow">Authority ledger</p><div><section><strong>System did</strong><span>Normalize, evaluate, preserve evidence, and prepare governed artifacts.</span></section><section><strong>Matthew directed</strong><span>Operating model, evidence architecture, decision boundaries, and validation.</span></section><section><strong>Human authority remained</strong><span>Approval, candidate interpretation, and application decisions.</span></section></div></aside>
    </header>

    <section class="joe-evidence-ledger shell" aria-label="Job Opportunity Engine evidence at a glance">
      <article><p class="eyebrow">Problem</p><p>Job evaluation and preparation can drift into inconsistent decisions, unsupported claims, and weak evidence traceability.</p></article>
      <article><p class="eyebrow">System</p><p>Private, local-first governed career operations for collection, deterministic evaluation, evidence-bound preparation, private artifact custody, and human review.</p></article>
      <article><p class="eyebrow">Verified</p><strong>180 / 180</strong><span>Passing automated tests at the latest clean public checkpoint.</span></article>
      <article><p class="eyebrow">Boundary</p><p>No autonomous submission, browser automation, production SaaS, or live model-backed generation.</p></article>
    </section>

    <section class="joe-section joe-problem shell" aria-labelledby="problem-title"><div class="joe-section-label"><p class="eyebrow">01 · The problem</p></div><div class="joe-section-body"><h2 id="problem-title">Useful automation begins with a trustworthy record of reality.</h2><p class="joe-lead">AI can quickly recommend roles or draft application language. The difficult part is ensuring that a recommendation, match, or generated claim is grounded in verified information and remains subject to human judgment.</p><div class="joe-principles"><p>What job is actually being considered?</p><p>What can be supported by candidate evidence?</p><p>Which gaps are material—and which are learnable?</p><p>What may be prepared, and what must remain a human decision?</p></div></div></section>

    <section class="joe-section joe-role shell" aria-labelledby="role-title"><div class="joe-section-label"><p class="eyebrow">02 · Matthew’s role</p></div><div class="joe-section-body"><h2 id="role-title">Directing the system, not claiming the keyboard.</h2><p>Matthew Ralph defined the product and system architecture, requirements, decision boundaries, evidence/state models, governance, validation criteria, implementation direction, and human-review controls. His role is that of a business systems and AI transformation operator: translating a consequential workflow into governed software and an inspectable operating model.</p><div class="authority-grid" aria-label="Authority boundary"><div><strong>Matthew</strong><span>Architecture, requirements, governance, validation</span></div><div><strong>AI coding agents</strong><span>Bounded implementation, inspection, testing, refinement</span></div><div><strong>Deterministic system</strong><span>Identity, evidence ownership, state, scoring, validation</span></div><div><strong>Human control</strong><span>Approval, claims, and external action</span></div></div><div class="joe-human-authority" aria-label="Human authority in Job Opportunity Engine"><p class="eyebrow">Human authority</p><p class="joe-role-statement"><strong>Matthew’s role:</strong> Designed the operating model, evidence architecture, decision boundaries, validation strategy, and human-approval controls; directed bounded agent implementation and testing against those requirements.</p><div class="joe-authority-division"><div><p class="eyebrow">System / agents</p><p>Deterministic validation and state tracking; bounded implementation, testing, and refinement; and surfacing evidence or conflict within repository and task constraints.</p></div><div><p class="eyebrow">What required human judgment</p><ul><li>Accept or reject evidence</li><li>Resolve ambiguous or stale state</li><li>Approve claims and preparation readiness</li><li>Decide whether external action may proceed</li></ul></div></div></div><p class="joe-note">AI coding agents performed substantial bounded implementation, inspection, testing, and refinement under repository controls and human review. They did not independently decide what was true, what the system could authorize, or when an external action should occur.</p></div></section>

    <section class="joe-section joe-system shell" aria-labelledby="system-title"><div class="joe-section-label"><p class="eyebrow">03 · Current system model</p></div><div class="joe-section-body"><h2 id="system-title">A controlled path from intake to human review.</h2><p>The implemented core preserves context, preparation authority, and decision traceability—not an autonomous job-application agent.</p><div class="workflow-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Current implemented workflow from intake through deterministic evaluation, frozen preparation, claim validation, private custody, and human review, with final submission marked outside runtime"><div class="workflow-row"><span>ATS / manual intake</span><i>→</i><span>Normalize + verify</span><i>→</i><span>Requirements</span><i>→</i><span>Evidence + capabilities</span></div><div class="workflow-row"><span>Deterministic evaluation</span><i>→</i><span>Rank + gate</span><i>→</i><span>Preparation command</span><i>→</i><span>Frozen packet</span></div><div class="workflow-row"><span>Claim validation</span><i>→</i><span>Private artifact custody</span><i>→</i><span>NEEDS_HUMAN / REVIEW_READY</span><i>→</i><span>Human review</span></div><div class="workflow-future"><span>Outside runtime</span><p>Broad external search automation · automated final submission</p></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="joe-section joe-governance shell" aria-labelledby="governance-title"><div class="joe-section-label"><p class="eyebrow">04 · Governance model</p></div><div class="joe-section-body"><h2 id="governance-title">AI proposes. Evidence proves. Humans approve.</h2><p>Candidate evidence is canonical and profile-isolated. Capability assessments may be proposed, but an interpretation becomes eligible for matching only when it is supported by linked evidence and approved by a human.</p><div class="evidence-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Evidence governance sequence"><div><b>1</b><strong>Career evidence</strong><span>Source material stays distinct from generated language.</span></div><div><b>2</b><strong>Governed assessment</strong><span>Capability interpretation is tied to appropriate evidence.</span></div><div><b>3</b><strong>Human approval</strong><span>Authority is explicit, rather than inferred from a model output.</span></div><div><b>4</b><strong>Eligible matching</strong><span>Only approved evidence may inform evaluation or preparation.</span></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="joe-section joe-preparation shell" aria-labelledby="preparation-title"><div class="joe-section-label"><p class="eyebrow">05 · Preparation authority</p></div><div class="joe-section-body"><h2 id="preparation-title">Preparation cannot silently drift from its verified basis.</h2><p>An eligible opportunity enters preparation through deterministic checks. The system freezes the job, evaluation, approved evidence, capability, and resume-baseline basis into an authoritative packet; proposed claims are validated against that basis before private artifacts can reach a review state.</p><div class="joe-principles"><p><strong>Frozen packet</strong><br />The reviewed basis is explicit rather than reconstructed later.</p><p><strong>Visible divergence</strong><br />Changed underlying state sends preparation back to human reconciliation.</p><p><strong>Private custody</strong><br />Artifacts and lineage stay private and profile-scoped.</p><p><strong>Review states</strong><br /><code>NEEDS_HUMAN</code> and <code>REVIEW_READY</code> do not authorize submission.</p></div><p class="joe-note">JOE also includes a candidate-scoped local review interface for inspecting jobs, evaluations, preparation state, supporting explanations, and review status. It is validated with synthetic tests; it is not a production SaaS.</p></div></section>

    <section class="joe-section joe-decisions shell" aria-labelledby="decisions-title"><div class="joe-section-label"><p class="eyebrow">06 · Design decisions</p></div><div class="joe-section-body"><h2 id="decisions-title">The controls are the product.</h2><div class="decision-records"><article><p class="eyebrow">Decision 01</p><h3>Generated output is not authoritative evidence</h3><dl><div><dt>Why</dt><dd>A polished résumé bullet or application draft does not become true simply because a system generated it.</dd></div><div><dt>Risk prevented</dt><dd>Unsupported claims being treated as candidate truth.</dd></div><div><dt>Consequence</dt><dd>Claims remain traceable to governed evidence.</dd></div></dl></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Decision 02</p><h3>Technical fluency is not software-engineering identity</h3><dl><div><dt>Why</dt><dd>The model distinguishes technical or program ownership from hands-on production implementation.</dd></div><div><dt>Risk prevented</dt><dd>Flattering but unsupported capability inflation.</dd></div><div><dt>Consequence</dt><dd>Systems or program evidence does not automatically establish software-engineering evidence.</dd></div></dl></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Decision 03</p><h3>Application state and outcome are distinct</h3><dl><div><dt>Why</dt><dd>A submission remains a submission even when a later outcome is rejection.</dd></div><div><dt>Risk prevented</dt><dd>Loss of lifecycle integrity.</dd></div><div><dt>Consequence</dt><dd>Later analysis can distinguish the submission event from its outcome.</dd></div></dl></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Decision 04</p><h3>AI judgment and software authority are separated</h3><dl><div><dt>Why</dt><dd>AI may assist interpretation while deterministic controls preserve critical state and decision rules.</dd></div><div><dt>Risk prevented</dt><dd>Model output silently becoming system authority.</dd></div><div><dt>Consequence</dt><dd>Identity, evidence ownership, lifecycle state, validation, and critical decision rules remain controlled.</dd></div></dl></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="joe-section joe-walkthrough shell" aria-labelledby="walkthrough-title"><div class="joe-section-label"><p class="eyebrow">07 · Synthetic walkthrough</p></div><div class="joe-section-body"><h2 id="walkthrough-title">A fictional example of depth-aware matching.</h2><p class="joe-note">This is an illustrative, fictional scenario. It is not a candidate record, application, or real job evaluation.</p><div class="depth-comparison"><article class="depth-match"><p class="eyebrow">Requirement A · program ownership</p><blockquote>“Lead deployment of agentic workflows across business operations. Partner with engineering and security. Establish governance, human-in-the-loop controls, evaluation frameworks, and operational readiness.”</blockquote><p><strong>Recognized concepts:</strong> Agentic Workflow Design · AI Governance · Human-in-the-Loop Design · Technical Program Direction</p><span class="depth-label">Technical fluency or program ownership</span></article><article class="depth-gap"><p class="eyebrow">Requirement B · hands-on implementation</p><blockquote>“Build distributed LLM inference services in production Python.”</blockquote><p><strong>Different classification:</strong> hands-on technical implementation. Systems or program evidence does not automatically establish software-engineering evidence.</p><span class="depth-label">Hands-on technical implementation</span></article></div></div></section>

    <section class="joe-section joe-validation shell" aria-labelledby="validation-title"><div class="joe-section-label"><p class="eyebrow">08 · Current state</p></div><div class="joe-section-body"><h2 id="validation-title">Implemented as a private, local-first career-operations system.</h2><div class="joe-checkpoint-pair"><article><p class="eyebrow">Clean public checkpoint</p><strong>180 / 180</strong><span>Passing automated tests at the latest clean public checkpoint. It does not represent active private development.</span><p class="checkpoint-note">Repository-level private-data policy check and Git diff check passed at that checkpoint.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Current boundary</p><strong>Human-controlled final action</strong><span>Private and local-first. Approval and final external action remain outside automated runtime scope.</span><p class="checkpoint-note">No autonomous application submission, browser automation, production SaaS, or live model-backed generation.</p></article></div><aside class="evidence-links" aria-labelledby="joe-evidence-title"><p class="eyebrow">Public documentation</p><h3 id="joe-evidence-title">Inspect public evidence</h3><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/matthew-ralph-work-samples/blob/main/job-opportunity-engine/synthetic-walkthrough.md">Evaluation walkthrough <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/matthew-ralph-work-samples/blob/main/job-opportunity-engine/preparation-lifecycle.md">Preparation lifecycle <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/matthew-ralph-work-samples/blob/main/job-opportunity-engine/design-decisions.md">Design decisions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li><li><a href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/matthew-ralph-work-samples/blob/main/job-opportunity-engine/validation-snapshot.md">Validation snapshot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li></ul></aside></div></section>

    <section class="joe-section joe-boundary shell" aria-labelledby="boundary-title"><div class="joe-section-label"><p class="eyebrow">09 · Scope boundary</p></div><div class="joe-section-body"><h2 id="boundary-title">Built for disciplined progress, not false autonomy.</h2><div class="scope-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Current</p><ul><li>Governed ATS and manual intake</li><li>Normalization, identity, verification, and deduplication</li><li>Evidence-bound evaluation, capability matching, and deterministic scoring</li><li>Preparation orchestration, frozen packets, private artifacts, and human review</li></ul></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Not currently automated</p><ul><li>Broad web search</li><li>Live model-backed generation and browser application</li><li>Production document QA and final application submission</li></ul></div></div><p class="joe-closing">The point is not to remove human responsibility from a consequential workflow. It is to make the information, choices, and boundaries that support human judgment more reliable.</p></div></section>
  </article>
